A||||6||Philphine||engine position and dogbone||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||09-15-2001||09:07 PM||||<BR>got some replacement v6 dogbone bushings from the fiero store (pretty quick considering the weeks events). when i took the dogbone off the engine moved forward enough to make the dogbone pretty hard to put back. i needed a crowbar and had to pull the engine back 1/2-3/4" to line the bolt up again. i had to do the same with my 4cyl. but not as far. normal? thanks for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||frankshel||09-15-2001||09:34 PM||||Normal.....All you have to do is put the transmission in neutral to remove the pressure on the transmission VS the engine. The engine will easily move back and forth with the pressure removed...ask me....I thought the same thing once when I was replacing the dog bone. Then I found out the way to do it. Good luck in the future. I own 5 Fiero's and have come across about everything there is. If I can be of more help in the future, my E mail address is:  shelfran@hotmail.com<BR>Frank Sheldon<BR>Ticonderoga, NY||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||09:50 PM||||What Frankshel said.  I just installed the Fiero Stores Ultimate Dogbone today.  I always leave my car in gear and forgot to slip it into neutral until I couldn't get the damn bolt in place.  Pulled the tranny out of gear and I was able to move the engine more than I needed to.  Piece of cake.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||09-15-2001||11:29 PM||||ok thanks. trying to put the gt i got on the road and didn't want an unexpected surprise. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mickey_Moose||09-16-2001||10:43 AM||||does one run into this problem when they have a auto?<P>thanks<BR>Tim<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||87GTZ34||09-16-2001||01:09 PM||||Mickey - Yes...  It is the weight of the car 'rocking' the drivetrain.  When the drivetrain is neutral, you still need a crowbar as there is an offset by design.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||09-16-2001||03:28 PM||||I just place a large block of wood on the top of a floor jack and lift by the pan till holes line up. The block spreads out the pressure and doesnt do any damage at all to pan.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 09-16-2001).]||||reg||1
